---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Adega",
  servesCuisine: ["Mediterranean", "Seafood"],
  priceRange: "$$$",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "2017 E 9th St",
    addressLocality: "Cleveland",
    addressRegion: "OH",
    postalCode: "44115",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Mediterranean fine-dining restaurant inside the Metropolitan at The 9 in downtown Cleveland, known for seafood and a strong wine program.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Adega Menu Guide (2026) — Cleveland's Mediterranean Gem"
  description="An independent guide to Adega at the Metropolitan at The 9 in Cleveland: Mediterranean seafood dishes, the Monday half-price wine tradition, and visiting tips. Facts reported as of October 2026."
  path="/adega-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/adega-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/adega-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of Adega's refined Mediterranean dining room in Cleveland"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Downtown Cleveland, Ohio
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Adega at the Metropolitan at The 9 — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">By <span class="font-semibold text-ink">Firoz Khan</span> <span class="text-gold-dark">&middot;</span> FK Digital Media</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      Adega is the Mediterranean fine-dining restaurant inside the Metropolitan at The 9 at
      2017 East 9th Street in downtown Cleveland. It built its reputation on seafood and a
      serious wine program — Cleveland Magazine gave it a Silver Spoon Award — and it remains
      one of the city's most-honored hotel dining rooms. Below is our independent walkthrough
      of the menu's shape, what to expect price-wise, and how to plan a visit. Everything is
      written in our own words; we are candid below about which price figures are current and
      which come from older published reviews.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">2017 E 9th St, Cleveland, OH 44115 (inside the Metropolitan at The 9)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Mediterranean, seafood-focused</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Upscale — entrées historically in the $28–$52 range</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Known for</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Bouillabaisse, Iberico pork chop, Monday half-price wine bottles</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Recommended; the room is small and fine-dining formal</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Dress code</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Smart — this is Cleveland's dress-up hotel dining room</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>The menu, by course</h2>
      <p>
        Adega's menu is built around the Mediterranean coast: fish and shellfish first, then
        pork, lamb, and beef, with olive oil, citrus, and herbs doing the heavy lifting. The
        dishes that recur across published reviews include a bouillabaisse, pan-roasted trout,
        pork tenderloin medallions, and an Iberico pork chop — a menu of European technique
        rather than Cleveland comfort.
      </p>
      <p>
        Older published reviews put individual dish prices at roughly <strong>$27 for the
        trout</strong>, <strong>$28 for pork tenderloin medallions</strong>, <strong>$45 for the
        Iberico pork chop</strong>, and <strong>$52 for the bouillabaisse</strong>. We label
        these as dated because they come from earlier published reviews — the current menu's
        prices should be confirmed directly with the restaurant before you visit.
      </p>

      <h2>The wine program</h2>
      <p>
        Wine is half the reason to come. Adega earned a Wine Spectator award, and the tradition
        of half-price bottles on Mondays has made it a local ritual: dinner on a Monday is the
        savvy move if you're buying wine. Expect a list weighted toward Old World bottles that
        suit the Mediterranean menu.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The signature:</strong> the bouillabaisse — it's the dish the restaurant's reputation rests on.</li>
        <li><strong>The value play:</strong> the pork tenderloin medallions, historically the most reasonably priced entrée.</li>
        <li><strong>The timing:</strong> go Monday, order the Iberico pork chop, and drink half-price wine with it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Confirm current prices.</strong> We could not verify a current published menu — call the restaurant for today's figures before budgeting.</li>
        <li><strong>Monday is the night</strong> if wine matters to you; it's the half-price-bottle tradition that locals plan around.</li>
        <li><strong>Occasion dining:</strong> this is the special-occasion pick of downtown Cleveland — anniversaries, proposals, and client dinners.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        Dish prices above come from <strong>older published reviews</strong> and may have
        changed — we could not verify a current menu, so treat them as historical context,
        not current figures. Always confirm prices with the restaurant before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-ohio/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to Ohio hotel restaurants</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
